          <customprops/>
          <polygon/>
          <id>Point05</id>
          <title>作品簡介/ Artwork Introduction</title>
          <description>無題/ Untitled

《無題》以油彩繪製而成，畫中遠景是美麗的山群，前景是一群共舞的人們。這幅畫靈感來自謝貽娟母親過去所任教的嘉義竹崎一帶的風景，源於她自童年到成長期的經驗。本作也是她尚未轉入抽象之前、較爲早期也較為具象的風景作品，畫中可見嘉義的自然、山脈，以及人文風情，也是她與嘉義的深刻連結。對謝貽娟來說，嘉義是「適合歸返、療癒、作畫和找尋自我的地方」。

The oil painting Untitled delineates a beautiful mountain range in the background and a group of dancing figures in the foreground. This painting draws inspiration from the landscapes of Jhuci in Chiayi, where Jo Hsieh’s mother once taught, as well as from her childhood and formative experiences. Created before her transition into abstraction, this is one of Hsieh’s earlier and more figurative landscape paintings. The natural scenery, mountain forms, and cultural imagery illustrated in the work reflect her deep connection to Chiayi. For Hsieh, Chiayi is “a place for returning, healing, painting, and self-discovery.”</description>
          <linktype>info</linktype>
          <linksubtype>unknown</linksubtype>
          <skinid>ht_info</skinid>
