          <customprops/>
          <polygon/>
          <id>Point03</id>
          <title>加與減/ More and Less</title>
          <description>在創作中，藝術家總在嘗試之間進行加與減。李錦繡跳脫學院訓練，於創作中借用書法筆勢、展現線條動態，也運用日常物件，在畫面中融入光影、留白與挖空等方式，實驗空間與形體的關係。同時李錦繡也致力藝術教育，將日常融入藝術，她在幼兒園的現地製作與個人創作，亦擅長以金屬、磚瓦、衣物等為媒材，轉化日常為造境，展現物我之間的流動與共感。

謝貽娟善用粉末、纖維與版畫等媒材，以線條與幾何組構畫面，將水、天、藍化為形式語彙。她的創作展現反覆、緩慢與細膩的勞動感，尤能以來回的線條、重複的形狀、牽引的色塊，組織豐富的音樂與律動性。此外，速寫本與草圖則記錄著日復一日的實驗過程與思考痕跡，亦為面對自我的持續練習。

本區納入蔡志賢與王怡婷的回應創作，分別以雕塑與自然材質介入，延伸兩位藝術家的創作思路，讓觀者不僅看到作品，更能體驗藝術家的實踐精神。

In the creative process, artists are always experimenting with adding more or less. Lii Jiin Shiow broke away from academic training and drew on calligraphy strokes to express dynamic lines in her works. She also incorporated everyday objects into her paintings, using light and shadow, negative space, and hollowing out to experiment with the relationship between space and form. In addition to her creative practice, Lii was dedicated to art education, integrating everyday life into her art. In her site-specific works for the kindergarten and her personal creations, she masterfully employed materials such as metal, bricks, tiles, and clothes to transform everyday life into a constructed environment, through which she illustrated the flow and empathy between objects and herself.
Jo Hsieh skillfully used powders, fibers, prints, and other media, composing her works with lines and geometric elements to transform water, sky, and blue into a vocabulary of forms. Her works exude a repeated, slow, and delicate sense of labor. She was particularly adept at using back-and-forth lines, repeated shapes, and interplaying color patches to create rich musicality and rhythm. Moreover, her sketchbooks and drafts, which document the day-to-day processes of experimentation and traces of thought, reveal a continuous practice of self-reflection.
This section also features Tsai Chih-hsien and Wang Yi-ting, who respond to the exhibition using sculptures and natural materials, respectively. Their works extend the creative concepts of Lii and Hsieh, inviting viewers not only to appreciate their works but also to experience their spirit of practice.   </description>
          <linktype>info</linktype>
          <linksubtype>unknown</linksubtype>
          <skinid>ht_info</skinid>
