          <id>Point07</id>
          <title>作品簡介/ Artwork Introduction</title>
          <description>謝貽娟一直以來都展現出對於水、天空、大自然的興趣，也用各種形式表現天空和水的型態、自然與自我的關係，她的作品中也經常以「手」搭配物件和環境。本件照相腐蝕版畫《Space Form III》，表現了一隻手的探觸，以「手」的介入影射創作的過程，手也彷彿代表謝貽娟的自我，在水波及光暈中有如同心圓一般散開，於有限空間延伸，展現自我的渺小存在以及與自然的無窮盡之對話。

Consistently drawn to themes of water, sky, and nature, Jo Hsieh presented the forms of sky and water through various means, reflecting on the relationship between nature and the self. In her works, the image of the hand frequently appears alongside objects and environmental elements. In the photo etching Space Form III, a hand is shown reaching outward. This gesture of intervention suggests the creative process, with the hand serving as a symbol of the artist herself. Amid ripples and halos that spread like concentric circles, the hand extends within a confined space, evoking the smallness of the self and its endless dialogue with nature. </description>
          <linktype>info</linktype>
          <linksubtype>unknown</linksubtype>
          <skinid>ht_info</skinid>
