          </next>
          <customprops/>
          <polygon/>
          <id>Point05</id>
          <title>作品資訊/ Artwork Information</title>
          <description>呼吸
Breathing
2025
本裝置作品以「繪畫線條」為核心，運用臺灣桂竹與黃銅線構成懸浮於空間中的不規則圓形結構。線條如同未完成的手稿樂譜，交錯牽引，映照著觀者與作品間無形的節奏與氣流。
素材使用了李錦繡所留下的教材紙張及黃銅片，紙張代表記憶殘片，黃銅則賦予視覺律動感。結構設計呼應謝貽娟手稿中的音樂性線條，透過纖維質感與金屬光澤，創造出視覺與材質雙重律動的「無聲音樂」。整體呈現持續呼吸的空間書寫，邀請觀者透過凝視與移動，感知視覺與身體之間的微妙共鳴。
Centering on the idea of “drawn lines,” this installation features a floating, irregular circular structure made of Makino bamboo and brass wire. The lines, intertwining and pulling against one another, resemble an unfinished musical manuscript, echoing the invisible rhythms and airflows between the viewer and the work.
This work incorporates paper and brass pieces from the lesson materials left by Lii Jiin Shiow. The paper serves as fragments of memory, while the brass gives a sense of visual rhythm. The structural design echoes the musical lines found in Jo Hsieh’s manuscripts, using the fibrous texture and the metal luster to create a “silent music” shaped by both visual and material rhythms. Altogether, the work represents a spatial composition in constant breath, inviting viewers to sense a subtle resonance between vision and the body through gaze and motion.</description>
