          </next>
          <customprops/>
          <polygon/>
          <id>Point04</id>
          <title>作品介紹/ Artwork Introduction</title>
          <description>對話/ Conversation

本作為李錦繡於1990年代後常見之居家空間主題之作，深刻表現了空間中的多樣物件與多重視點，畫中灰色調的場域回應了李錦繡對「存在」的體察，在「模糊」與「灰色」之間，物件凌亂卻又有各自的位置，涵蓋了交流與凝視。

作品具有第一人稱到第三人稱的感知方式，也是李錦繡一貫創作的特質。畫外擺放的兩把椅子，以「第三人稱」的方式觀照著繪畫，像是一個旁觀者和局外人；而兩把椅子同時也表徵李錦繡的自我，椅子是讓人乘坐的物件，也是人以「第一人稱」參與其所處環境的定位和視點；最後，《對話〉這件作品的名稱以第二人稱定名，在面對之間，話語、視線交流，讓我和物的存在，於空間中有更多遐想。 

Focusing on domestic interiors, a recurring theme in Lii Jiin Shiow’s work since the 1990s, this piece delineates a rich array of objects within the space from multiple perspectives. The gray-toned setting reflects Lii’s contemplation of existence. Within the obscurity and grayness, the seemingly scattered objects are nonetheless purposefully placed, implying a sense of interaction and mutual gaze.

The work shifts between first-person and third-person perspectives, a consistent characteristic of Lii’s artistic approach. The two chairs positioned outside the painting are like bystanders or outsiders, engaging with the painting from a third-person point of view. At the same time, they symbolize the artist herself, not only as functional objects for sitting, but also as markers of a first-person presence within the environment. Finally, the title of this work, Conversation, invokes a second-person engagement. Through this encounter, words and gazes are exchanged, allowing room for reflection on the existence of both the self and the object.</description>
          <linktype>info</linktype>
          <linksubtype>unknown</linksubtype>
          <skinid>ht_info</skinid>
          <type>point</type>
          <distance>0</distance>
          <distanceauto>1</distanceauto>
          <autoplace>0</autoplace>
          <use3d>0</use3d>
          <width>0</width>
          <height>0</height>
        </hotspot>
        <hotspot>
          <position>
            <pan>-105.61</pan>
            <tilt>14.9</tilt>
            <fov>10</fov>
          </position>
          <next>
            <pan>0</pan>
            <tilt>0</tilt>
            <fov>0</fov>
          </next>
          <customprops/>
          <polygon/>
          <id>Point05</id>
          <title>藝術家介紹/ Artist Introduction</title>
          <description>蔡志賢（1958-）
TSAI Chih-hsien
出身嘉義，鐵雕藝術家。擅長以「即成物」（found objects）進行創作，以焊接、拼組與重構，賦予物件新的生命。作品偏好抽象及半抽象，美學風格深沉且內斂。
Tsai Chih-hsien is a metal sculptor from Chiayi. Skillfully working with found objects, he gives them new life through welding, assemblage, and reconstruction. His works are primarily abstract or semi-abstract, characterized by a profound and understated aesthetic.</description>
          <linktype>info</linktype>
          <linksubtype>unknown</linksubtype>
          <safeurl>3F_w150_h230mm.pdf</safeurl>
          <target>_blank</target>
          <skinid>ht_info</skinid>
          <type>point</type>
          <distance>0</distance>
          <distanceauto>1</distanceauto>
          <autoplace>0</autoplace>
          <use3d>0</use3d>
          <width>0</width>
          <height>0</height>
        </hotspot>
        <hotspot>
          <position>
            <pan>-40.71</pan>
            <tilt>11.75</tilt>
            <fov>10</fov>
          </position>
          <next>
            <pan>0</pan>
            <tilt>0</tilt>
            <fov>0</fov>
          </next>
          <customprops/>
          <polygon/>
          <id>Point06</id>
          <title>作品介紹/ Artwork Introduction</title>
          <description>傍晚別離 Evening Farewell
等什麼呢 Waiting for What
還是忘記 Still Forgetting
2025
鐵雕和風有關，過度用力會傷了時間；凝視材料， 拆解與再造，羞澀且沉重的雙腿，浮上了聲響。
創作和意志有關，《傍晚別離》、《等什麼呢》、《還是忘記》，全是帶著語氣的一生懸命。
My metal sculptures are connected to the wind; too much force can wound time. I gaze into the materials, dismantling and reconstructing them. Shy and heavy legs resonate with sound.
Creative practice is driven by willpower. Evening Farewell, Waiting for What, and Still Forgetting all carry a distinct emotional tone, each created with all-out devotion.</description>
          <linktype>info</linktype>
          <linksubtype>unknown</linksubtype>
          <skinid>ht_info</skinid>
