          <id>Point04</id>
          <title>作品介紹/ Artwork Introduction</title>
          <description>線延伸出的那些漪
As Lines Are Drawn, Ripples Begin
2025
在李錦繡與謝貽娟的創作過程中那些素描練習與對於線條的思考，總是不斷地提問、練習與創造，她們的思路是交錯媒材、是纏繞故事、是鉤織時光、亦是紡捻生命。我在李錦繡留下的材料中找到了一根木製線軸，是纖維紡捻成紗線製成線筒時的支軸，它記錄著時代與產業的更迭。
我彷如看到了藝術家創作的核心，作品圍繞著藝術家的生命歷程而紡捻淬煉。因此透過線條與色彩呈現兩位藝術家的生命力，一根根管狀彩色編織垂懸而下，與地上的藍色織毯相互對話，藉此感受藝術家在作品中留下的能量、敘事與痕跡。似樹、似根、似水、似浪，致敬她們奉獻給創作的生命。
In the creative process of Lii Jiin Shiow and Jo Hsieh, their drawing studies and reflections on lines were acts of constant questioning, practicing, and making. Their ways of thinking intertwined media, entangled stories, wove time, and spun life. Among the materials Lii left behind, I discovered a wooden spool, which was once the core shaft used in spinning fibers into yarn for bobbin-making. It records the shifts of time and industry.
I feel as if I have seen the cores of the artists’ creative spirits, and my work is spun and refined around the threads of their life journeys. Through the renderings of lines and colors, their vitality is made visible. Tubular, colorful weavings hang down and enter into dialogue with the blue tapestry on the ground, evoking the energy, narrative, and traces the artists have left within their works. Like trees, roots, water, and waves, this work is a tribute to the lives they devoted to art-making.</description>
          <linktype>info</linktype>
          <linksubtype>unknown</linksubtype>
          <safeurl>_w150_h315mm.pdf</safeurl>
          <target>_blank</target>
